;;; A premise-less derivation is never recorded as an alternative — **W25**,
;;; register row `W25/guard-only-second` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), open.
;;; Its control is `guard-only-first.ein`: the same program with `early` reading
;;; `(pp ?x)`, which a rule derives from `(p ?x)`, so that `w` arrives first
;;; (its header).
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two candidates, `(p a)` and `(p2 a)`. Committing `(p a)` derives `(false)`
;;; twice: by `early`, from `(p a) (b a) (seed a)`, and by `w`, a rule with a
;;; parameter and no premise, whose activator `(w a)` `mk` derives from `(p a)`.
;;; `early` fires first: its candidate queues when `(p a)` is committed, before
;;; `mk` has derived `w`'s activator (both conclude `(false)`, and the agenda
;;; fires them in the written and arrival order, Q-M1f.313).
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `{(p a)}` is dead, and its core is the smallest frontier over its
;;; derivations (`glossary.md` § Smallest contradiction frontier): `w`'s rests
;;; on its activator `(w a)`, which a node derived from `(p a)` and which a core
;;; follows (Q-M1e2.12), so the core is `(p a)` alone, as the control reports.
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `Saturator::record_alternative` returns before recording a firing with no
;;; premise, and `Kb::record_justification` refuses one (the rule for an engine
;;; writeback), so `w`'s derivation, arriving second, is never an alternative
;;; and the core is `early`'s three facts: N `{(p a)}`, core `(b a) (p a) (seed
;;; a)` (`ein solve FILE --dump-answer DIR`'s `nogoods.json` and `ein oracle
;;; FILE --dump DIR` at `94c75204`, release and debug alike; a store with no
;;; alternatives cap gives the same). Which rule fires first, by the written and
;;; arrival order, decides which core is reported. No corpus program writes the
;;; shape. The engine does not re-derive what the store does not keep, so the
;;; reported core stays `early`'s.

(relation seed T :why "{?1} is a seed") (relation p T :why "p holds of {?1}") (relation p2 T :why "p2 holds of {?1}") (relation w T :why "w holds of {?1}") (relation b T :why "b holds of {?1}")
(seed a) (b a)
(hrule g  () :match (seed ?x) :assert (p ?x) :why "guess that p holds of the seed {?x}")
(hrule g2 () :match (seed ?x) :assert (p2 ?x) :why "guess that p2 holds of the seed {?x}")
(rule early () :match (and (p ?x) (b ?x) (seed ?x)) :assert (false) :why "p and b both hold of the seed {?x}, which cannot be")
(rule mk () :match (p ?x) :assert (w ?x) :why "p holds of {?x}, so w holds of {?x}, switching rule w on for it")
(rule w (?n) :match (eq ?n a) :assert (false) :why "w holds of {?n} and {?n} is a, which cannot be")
